  <SubSection title="What is SNR?" id="What">
      <p>Signal to Noise Ratio or SNR is the ratio between the power (or amplitude squared) of a signal and the power of the surrounding noise. This is often determined in the frequency domain in order to isolate the frequency of the target signal and determine its power compared to the power of unwanted frequencies which are defined as noise.
